    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The fire in the hearth is nothing but grey ash now. Everything is... quiet. Too quiet. I'm sitting here among the rubble of what used to be the Great Hall, just staring at my hands. They're shaking. There's nothing left to defend, no kingdom to rebuild, and no one left to call my name. It feels like the ink has run dry on my life. Like there's just no point in turning the page anymore.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
